Rule 1 (inputs must be at least 2D and have identical shapes across all dims)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 2 (inputs must be numeric and share the same dtype: 1–10; prevents bool subtraction)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10 ∧ dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 3 (norm degree p must be at least 1)
{v_3: float} |= v_3 ≥ 1
>>
Rule 4 (epsilon must be non-negative)
{v_4: float} |= v_4 ≥ 0
>>
Rule 5 (if keepdim is true, the reduction dimension must exist)
{v_1: tensor, v_5: bool} |= if v_5 then ndim(v_1) ≥ 2
>>
Rule 6 (vector dimension (dim=1) must be positive for both inputs; helps avoid size-0 vs size-5 mismatches)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= shape(v_1, 1) > 0 ∧ shape(v_2, 1) > 0
